#
# DECISION: gate FAILED (R3, M1, GC1). Every failing criterion fails for ONE cause: the thermal solve's
# LinearSolveFailure from a BiCGSTAB breakdown near round-off (logs/12). Not a mesh-quality defect; not fixed
# in P12-MESH-004 (solver behaviour change outside the authorized scope without a separate decision).
#
# Informational only -- NOT gate evidence (these runs are not accepted by the gate): the smooth A = 0.05
# corrected runs' measured L2 orders, from fields whose thermal Picard loop stopped within max |dT| ~3e-8 of
# convergence (logs/12): 8->16 u 2.197 v 2.408 p 2.273 T 0.621; 16->32 u 2.161 v 2.367 p 2.011 T 0.861;
# 32->64 u 2.031 v 2.048 p 2.062 T 0.951.
#
# Unexpected findings (reported, not diagnosed -- the gate stopped the work):
#  (a) cell-scale irregular meshes (D2 / rough family): velocity and pressure errors grow steeply with the
#      irregularity (D2 Q1, skewness 0.064: u L2 5.7x, p L2 58.8x Q0) and do NOT converge under refinement
#      (f = 0.15: u L2 2.19e-2 / 2.15e-2 / 1.39e-2 for n = 16 / 32 / 64, p L2 0.243 / 0.432 / 0.509; n = 64
#      SIMPLE MaxIterations 20000). Temperature on the same meshes converges (order 0.92). The uncorrected
#      recipe gives nearly the same u/v/p errors, so the non-orthogonal correction is not what differs.
#  (b) the uncorrected recipe (0 corrections) diverges (MomentumFailure) on the SMOOTH family at every
#      non-zero amplitude tested at n = 32 (17.7 deg upward) and at n >= 16 for A = 0.05, with relaxation
#      0.8/0.4; it converges on the rough family. Whether a lower relaxation changes this was not tested.
#  (c) the R5 "continuity contraction" metric (final / first continuity residual per iteration) is
#      uninformative (~1.000 everywhere: the zero initial field makes the first residual tiny); SIMPLE
#      iteration counts are the usable convergence-cost measure.
